<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 16 November, from 534 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/534">534 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian I publishes the second edition of the Codex Justinianus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> published the second edition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a>, known as the Codex Repetitae Praelectionis, which superseded the first after his new laws had left it out of date. It took effect on 30 December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1093">1093 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">933 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Margaret of Scotland dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret, wife of Malcolm III, died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> Castle days after learning that her husband and eldest son had been killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alnwick">Alnwick</a>. Celebrated for her piety and church reform, she was canonised in 1250.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1272">1272 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">754 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward I becomes King of England on Henry III's death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of King Henry III, Prince Edward, still travelling on the Ninth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a>, became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> as Edward I. He did not return to England for nearly two years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england">Edward I of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1491">1491 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">535 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An auto-da-fé at Ávila concludes the Holy Child of La Guardia case</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> auto-da-fé held outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avila">Ávila</a> ended with six conversos and two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> burnt at the stake. They had been accused in the case of the Holy Child of La Guardia, a medieval blood libel.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avila">Ávila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1532">1532 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">494 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pizarro captures the Inca ruler Atahualpa at Cajamarca</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a>'s force of fewer than 200 men ambushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a>'s retinue in the square of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cajamarca">Cajamarca</a>, killing thousands. Holding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> ruler captive gave the Spanish leverage over a vast empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1632">1632 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">394 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gustavus Adolphus is killed at the Battle of Lützen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Swedish army under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a>, supported by troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>, narrowly defeated an imperial force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albrecht-von-wallenstein">Albrecht von Wallenstein</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutzen-1632">Lützen</a>. Both sides suffered heavy casualties, and Gustavus himself was among the dead.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lutzen-1632">Battle of Lützen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manhattan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The British capture Fort Washington on Manhattan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and Hessian troops stormed Fort Washington, the last American stronghold on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>, and took about 2,800 prisoners. Washington's army retreated across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UNESCO's constitution is signed in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates of 37 countries signed the constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization</a>. It promotes cooperation in education, science and culture and lists World Heritage Sites.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1988">1988 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Benazir Bhutto's party wins Pakistan's general election</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> Peoples Party, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benazir-bhutto">Benazir Bhutto</a>, won the most seats in the first open election in over a decade. Weeks later she became the first woman to lead a Muslim-majority democracy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
